    description: "Sibling of INV-fosam (which fixed the 5 clean alias mismatches adonis/aspnetcore/next/vert.x/zio-http). The structural sweep (test_route_framework_yaml_reachability, 2026-07-07) found 12 route-emitting YAMLs unreachable from any import key; 5 were the INV-fosam mismatches. The other 7 are a DISTINCT class aliases cannot fix: CLASS B keyless (flask-restful/lumen/masonite/restify/scalatra — no LANGUAGE_FRAMEWORKS entry; MAY be manifest-reachable, unverified; if detected via import-only their routes drop); CLASS A' generic 'http' key (http4k/node-http). Currently EXEMPTED in _ROUTE_YAML_NO_IMPORT_KEY so the invariant stays green while catching NEW drift. Fix: verify each keyless YAML is manifest-reachable (add a manifest-detection test) or wire an import key; resolve the 'http' ambiguity with language-scoped keys; remove each from the exemption set as wired. Surfaced by the INV-fosam PR."  # 68ed
    fields:  # 68ed
      statement: "Every route-emitting framework YAML is reachable from a detection key (directly or via alias) or is verified reachable via manifest/package-name detection."  # 68ed
      root_cause: "LANGUAGE_FRAMEWORKS has NO import key for flask-restful/lumen/masonite/restify/scalatra (their route YAMLs are reachable only via manifest/package-name detection, UNVERIFIED), and http4k/node-http both map to the single generic key 'http' (one key cannot alias to two YAMLs). Aliases (the INV-fosam fix) cannot address either class."  # 68ed
